  "id": "MetaverseDomain",
  "title": "MetaverseDomain",
  "content": "- ### OntologyBlock\n  id:: metaversedomain-ontology\n  collapsed:: true\n\t- ontology:: true\n\t- term-id:: MV-7000\n\t- preferred-term:: MetaverseDomain\n\t- source-domain:: mv\n\t- status:: active\n\t- public-access:: true\n\t- definition:: The Metaverse Domain provides an ontological framework for interconnected digital platforms leveraging augmented, extended, and virtual realities to create immersive user experiences through multidimensional interactions. It encompasses virtual environments, avatar embodiment, spatial computing, digital economies, and the convergence of physical and virtual worlds where millions can simultaneously inhabit and interact in real-time regardless of physical distance.\n\t- maturity:: reviewed\n\t- owl:class:: mv:Metaversedomain\n\t- owl:role:: Domain\n\t- belongsToDomain:: [[TechnologyDomain]]\n\n## Relationships\n- ### Subdomains\n\t- [[VirtualReality]] - Fully immersive digital environments\n\t- [[AugmentedReality]] - Digital overlay on physical reality\n\t- [[ExtendedReality]] - Spectrum of mixed reality experiences\n\t- [[VirtualEconomies]] - Digital asset and currency systems\n\t- [[AvatarSystems]] - Virtual representation and embodiment\n\n- ### Related Concepts\n\t- [[SpatialComputing]] - 3D interaction and spatial awareness\n\t- [[DigitalTwin]] - Virtual replicas of physical entities\n\t- [[Interoperability]] - Cross-platform compatibility\n\t- [[DecentralizedTechnologies]] - Blockchain and distributed infrastructure\n\t- [[ArtificialIntelligence]] - NPC behaviors and content generation\n\t- [[HapticFeedback]] - Sensory immersion technologies\n\t- [[WebXR]] - Web-based immersive experiences\n\n- ### Key Technologies\n\t- [[ExtendedRealityXR]] - Primary enabling technology (73% of implementations)\n\t- [[BlockchainTechnology]] - Decentralized ownership and transactions\n\t- [[CloudComputing]] - Scalable infrastructure support\n\n## Metadata\n\n- **Last Updated**: 2025-12-29\n- **Review Status**: Reviewed and enriched\n- **References**: 167 pages reference this concept",
